# 9. SMART FARMER NOTIFICATION SYSTEM

Create a clear distinction between information, notification and action.

- Information Center: full details and sources.
- Notification Inbox: short updates and reminders.
- Today's Activities: actions the farmer should perform.

Do not duplicate the same content unnecessarily.

## A. In-app notification

The notification bell should open the Notification Inbox.

Support notifications for:

- Relevant disease advisories.
- Important farm-specific alerts.
- Action reminders.
- Newly assigned activities.
- Preventive-care schedules.
- Veterinary appointment updates.
- Important platform messages.

Every notification should route to the appropriate screen.

Reading a notification must not mark a farm activity as completed.

## B. SMS notification capability

Design the system architecture so that important farmer notifications can eventually be delivered through SMS.

Requirements:

- Phone number.
- Verification status.
- Farmer consent.
- Notification preferences.
- Relevant alert categories.
- Reminder preferences.
- Unsubscribe option.
- Delivery status where supported.

Do not send every reminder to every farmer.

Suggested priority:

- Relevant important official outbreak alert: potential priority SMS.
- Critical farm-specific action: SMS when appropriate.
- Routine preventive-care reminder: optional SMS.
- General DLS news: generally in-app only.
- General educational content: no routine SMS.

Use concise Bengali messages.

SMS must be sent through a secure backend and an authorized SMS gateway.

Never expose SMS provider credentials in frontend code.

Do not simulate actual delivery.

If no gateway is connected, label SMS functionality as planned/demo and preserve the integration point for future development.

Do not claim an SMS was sent or delivered unless confirmed by the provider.

## C. Notification frequency

Avoid notification fatigue.

- Do not repeatedly notify about an action already completed.
- Do not send reminders for non-applicable tasks.
- Avoid unnecessary repeated alerts.
- Respect farmer preferences and consent.
- Provide sensible reminder frequency.
- Support quiet hours where possible.

## D. Future communication channels

Keep the architecture extensible for future voice/IVR notifications.

Do not implement a fake voice-call feature.

